1. Create a 3-dimensional array in R to store the monthly sales of 4 products across 3 months and 2 branches. Perform the following operations: 
• Display the array and its dimensions. 
• Calculate the total sales for each product.  
• Find the maximum and minimum sales using appropriate built-in functions.
• Calculate the average sales for each branch.  

sales <- array(1:24, dim = c(4, 3, 2))

print(sales)
print(dim(sales))

print(rowSums(matrix(sales, nrow = 4)))

print(max(sales))
print(min(sales))

print(mean(sales[, , 1]))
print(mean(sales[, , 2]))
