2. Write a user-defined R function analyze_scores() that accepts a vector of student marks and returns: 
• Mean and median marks 
• Maximum and minimum marks 
• Standard deviation 
• Number of students scoring above the mean 
• Test the function using a suitable vector of 10 student marks. 

analyze_scores <- function(marks) {
  print(mean(marks))
  print(median(marks))
  print(max(marks))
  print(min(marks))
  print(sd(marks))
  print(sum(marks > mean(marks)))
}

marks <- c(60, 70, 80, 90, 50, 85, 75, 95, 65, 55)

analyze_scores(marks)

