3. Create a vector containing the names of 10 students. Using appropriate R functions:
• Convert all names to uppercase. 
• Find the number of characters in each name.
• Identify names having more than 6 characters. 
• Sort the names alphabetically. 
• Search for names containing a specified character or substring. 

names <- c("Amit", "Priyanka", "Rahul", "Sneha", "Nikita",
           "Sakshi", "Anjali", "Rohit", "Pooja", "Karan")

print(toupper(names))
print(nchar(names))
print(names[nchar(names) > 6])
print(sort(names))
print(grep("a", names, value = TRUE))
